> So how about some changes to this part of the prayer code.  Time
> between prayers should be based on what you do in the dungeon.  The
> base time should be a function of experience points since the last
> prayer, possibly normalized to the experience level of the player.
> This base time can then be modified by such factors as:  dungeon
> level, luck, current hps, current health, hunger status, alignment of
> monsters killed, etc.

Since we're on the subject, one thing I'd like to see added to the list
of modifying factors is some kind of "hit points delta".  By that I
mean, if you just were fighting some kind of vicious monster (those
mumakils (sp?) always seem to get me) and you just dropped 30 or 40 hit
points, you aren't going to get a chance to pray when you're hit points
get below 5.  Often, I die from one hit that takes away 30 or so hit
points.  I'm not sure how difficult it would be to implement this, but
it shouldn't be too hard.

